% Macros specific to this handout: objects the shared registry (econ-ark-tools, @resources/notation) lacks.
% Each is a bridge: it loads after econark-notation, so once the vendored registry defines the macro,
% the registry's definition wins; then delete the line here. The book defines each the same way, as
% course-local entries in its notation/course-local-math.yml (\PtyLab and \Ham as candidates for registry
% rows). Rule D (Chris, 2026-11-15) writes every object with a macro, so an object the registry lacks gets one here.
\providecommand{\PtyLab}{\mathrm{Z}}% labor-augmenting productivity
\providecommand{\Ham}{\mathcal{H}}% the (discounted) Hamiltonian
\providecommand{\vk}{\lambda}% the costate on capital, which is its marginal value: the book's \vk (qModel's lambda)

% Not notation. A note the book prints in its margin (a {margin} block), printed here as a footnote
% (Chris, 2026-11-14: "As a footnote"). check-book-sync.py compares it with the book's margin block.
\newcommand{\marginFootnote}[1]{\footnote{#1}}
